# Architecture

The executable loads the library and returns the CLI's exit status. The CLI uses
OptionParser and accepts injected output streams so behavior can be tested
without a real terminal. Version data has one source in
lib/<%= @require_path %>/version.rb.

The gemspec allows only runtime Ruby files, the executable and selected public
documents into the package. It declares OptionParser as a runtime dependency.
The maintenance toolkit, tests, linters and audit tool are development dependencies
and are not required to run an installed copy of the CLI.

The Rakefile delegates repository, package and release operations to ruby-repo-kit.
The local .ruby-repo.yml declares project identity and the CI check names. CI
jobs remain in this repository. Ruby lint rules inherit the versioned shared
preset, with project-specific overrides in .rubocop.yml.

There are no generated runtime artifacts initially. The generate and
generate:check tasks deliberately have no work. When introducing a generated
manual or similar artifact, implement these tasks and declare its paths in
.ruby-repo.yml.

The scaffold is a starting point. No process reapplies it over application code,
tests or documentation. Dependency upgrades change shared maintenance behavior;
changes to local integration files require review.
